   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law and the economic development law, in relation to annual awards recognizing certain New York farms, businesses and institutions",
    "basePrintNo": "S1333",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1333-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §309, Ag & Mkts L; amd §100, Ec Dev L",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1333\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the agriculture and markets law and\nthe economic development law, in relation to annual awards recognizing\ncertain New York farms, businesses and institutions\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nWould establish an agriculture and food awards program in the New York\nState Department of Agriculture and Markets and have the Commissioner\ncoordinate with the Department of Economic Development on their award\nprogram.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThe bill would amend the Agriculture and Markets Law to add a new\nsubdivision 9 to § 309 to have the Advisory Council on Agriculture\nmake award nominations to the Commissioner to recognize exceptional\nperformance and success by New York farms, agricultural and food\nbusinesses, and institutions in producing, processing, marketing,\nand/or promoting New York farm and food products. The award categories\nwould include: (a) innovative and unique farm products developed for\nfood, beverages, or horticulture; (b) agritourism; (c) foods or\nbeverages processed or manufactured from New York farm products;(d)\nretail food stores; (e) restaurants and other food service businesses;\nand, (f) education, health care and residential institutions. In\naddition to these awards, the Commissioner and Advisory Council would\ncoordinate with the Department of Economic Development, which also has\nauthority to recommend awards for New York farms and farm products.\n\nThe bill would also amend subdivision 18c of § 100 to have the\nCommissioner of Economic Development coordinate with the Commissioner\nof Agriculture and Markets to determine which department shall make\nnominations for awards in categories that may be similar to those\nlisted in subdivision nine of § 309 of the agriculture and markets\nlaw.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nNew York farmers, food processors and craft beverage producers are\nproducing high quality foods and beverages that are often recognized\nnationally and internationally. These fruits and vegetables, craft\ncheeses, yogurts, ice creams, specialty meats, wines, beers, ciders\nand spirits, and dozens of other products deserve state recognition by\nour State government. This legislation would provide a mechanism for\nthe Commissioner of Agriculture and Markets to not only provide awards\nto the farmers, manufacturers and processors that produce these\nexceptional products using locally-sourced ingredients, but also the\nbusinesses that make a special effort to market and promote them.\nThese awards could also be presented to restaurants, food retailers,\nand schools and colleges that feature and promote New York farm foods.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2015-16: S.7745/A.,9756 Referred to Agriculture\nA.9756 Passed Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS : To be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
